Subject: [PATCH 02486/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A1
 (HEADLINE; oracle-distinct EFFICIENCY moat, STRONGER function class) --
 LLM-GENERATED ACTION-COST HEURISTICS (arXiv:2503.18809 VERIFIED 'Classical
 Planning with LLM-Generated Heuristics: Challenging the State of the Art with
 Python Code', Correa/Pereira/Seipp). .403 (exp4364) PROVED a LINEAR learned
 A* action-cost heuristic COMPOUNDS (held-out env-actions 25->16,
 positive-control-passed, reproduction-gated, DEPLOYED into arc_solver_kit,
 verifier_is_oracle=false) -- but the stronger LLM-generated-PROGRAM arm did
 NOT run (llm_heuristic_arm.ran=false). This is the flagged_for_v404 HEADLINE:
 does a STRONGER function class deepen the efficiency moat? The codex agent
 (the proposer -- NO nested CodexProposer) writes several DOMAIN-DEPENDENT
 Python heuristic functions h(state)->cost-to-go per ARC game, selects the
 strongest by GREEDY-BEST-FIRST-SEARCH on TRAINING levels (the 2503.18809
 method), then evaluates on FRESH HELD-OUT levels vs the DEPLOYED linear
 heuristic (exp4364). Skeptic-proof by construction: STATIC-LEAKAGE analysis
 on every generated program (reject any that reads answer cells / env
 internals / hard-codes a level layout), a reproduction gate on every counted
 plan (arc_solver_kit.reproduce), and a fixed held-out split. Emit
 llm_heuristic_beats_linear BARE bool := (the best CLEAN LLM-generated
 heuristic reduces held-out actions-to-solve BELOW the deployed linear
 heuristic AND static_leakage_clean AND every counted plan reproduces).
 verifier_is_oracle=false (the heuristic ESTIMATES cost-to-go; the executable
 env defines the win -- oracle-distinct). A win = the efficiency moat DEEPENS
 (a stronger learned heuristic generalizes better); a CLEAN null (the linear
 cost is already near-optimal on our solved games) is decision-grade (the
 function class is settled). NO TRM training; CPU-offline search; the codex
 agent generates the programs (zero extra GGUF load).

